{
  "schema_version": "1.0",
  "encounter_id": "01234",
  "segments": [
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0001",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 0.72,
      "end_seconds": 3.99,
      "duration_seconds": 3.27,
      "text": "Hello, doctor. I think it's my turn."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0002",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 6.09,
      "end_seconds": 10.97,
      "duration_seconds": 4.88,
      "text": "You're alright, take a seat. What can I do for you?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0003",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 12.4,
      "end_seconds": 18.09,
      "duration_seconds": 5.69,
      "text": "so the thing is, I've got headaches in the morning"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0004",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 19.5,
      "end_seconds": 22.23,
      "duration_seconds": 2.73,
      "text": "How long has it been like this?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0005",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 23.07,
      "end_seconds": 25.03,
      "duration_seconds": 1.96,
      "text": "About... well, three days."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0006",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 26.26,
      "end_seconds": 37.26,
      "duration_seconds": 11.0,
      "text": "Okay, tell me a bit more about it: how bad it gets, how often, and whether anything makes it better or worse."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0007",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 40.97,
      "end_seconds": 46.43,
      "duration_seconds": 5.46,
      "text": "It happens a couple of times a week. It's mild, honestly."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0008",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 48.46,
      "end_seconds": 51.87,
      "duration_seconds": 3.41,
      "text": "Have you noticed anything else alongside it?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0009",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 53.01,
      "end_seconds": 72.86,
      "duration_seconds": 19.85,
      "text": "It usually comes with a pounding in my ears. The pounding in my ears? That's been for two months. About pounding in my ears, a seven out of ten, I suppose. It comes and goes."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0010",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 76.7,
      "end_seconds": 79.03,
      "duration_seconds": 2.33,
      "text": "Let me take your readings now."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0011",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 86.35,
      "end_seconds": 88.41,
      "duration_seconds": 2.06,
      "text": "Sit still for a moment..."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0012",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 105.28,
      "end_seconds": 114.27,
      "duration_seconds": 8.99,
      "text": "Okay: heart rate 75, blood pressure 153 over 100, saturation 96 percent, respiratory rate 17, temperature 36.6."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0013",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 118.41,
      "end_seconds": 119.84,
      "duration_seconds": 1.43,
      "text": "Is that normal?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0014",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 121.28,
      "end_seconds": 124.71,
      "duration_seconds": 3.43,
      "text": "Don't worry, we'll discuss it in a second."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0015",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 126.83,
      "end_seconds": 130.66,
      "duration_seconds": 3.83,
      "text": "alright, over here please and I'll take a look"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0016",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 132.73,
      "end_seconds": 134.19,
      "duration_seconds": 1.46,
      "text": "Fine by me."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0017",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 135.17,
      "end_seconds": 136.95,
      "duration_seconds": 1.78,
      "text": "let me feel here"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0018",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 151.8,
      "end_seconds": 157.31,
      "duration_seconds": 5.51,
      "text": "your heart sounds are normal and there is no swelling in your ankles"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0019",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 161.72,
      "end_seconds": 167.7,
      "duration_seconds": 5.98,
      "text": "Thank you, you can get dressed. Did you get chest pain or breathlessness?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0020",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 168.8,
      "end_seconds": 172.21,
      "duration_seconds": 3.41,
      "text": "no, no chest pain or breathlessness"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0021",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 173.91,
      "end_seconds": 177.8,
      "duration_seconds": 3.89,
      "text": "have you had leg swelling, by any chance?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0022",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 179.18,
      "end_seconds": 182.33,
      "duration_seconds": 3.15,
      "text": "Not at all, no leg swelling."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0023",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 183.17,
      "end_seconds": 185.73,
      "duration_seconds": 2.56,
      "text": "your breathing, any trouble there?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0024",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 186.43,
      "end_seconds": 187.41,
      "duration_seconds": 0.98,
      "text": "breathing's normal"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0025",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 188.02,
      "end_seconds": 190.38,
      "duration_seconds": 2.36,
      "text": "Anything unusual with passing urine?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0026",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 192.17,
      "end_seconds": 193.65,
      "duration_seconds": 1.48,
      "text": "nothing there, no"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0027",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 207.47,
      "end_seconds": 208.67,
      "duration_seconds": 1.2,
      "text": "any previous surgeries?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0028",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 209.87,
      "end_seconds": 211.96,
      "duration_seconds": 2.09,
      "text": "No, not at all."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0029",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 221.6,
      "end_seconds": 224.19,
      "duration_seconds": 2.59,
      "text": "Do you take any regular medication?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0030",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 225.47,
      "end_seconds": 226.69,
      "duration_seconds": 1.22,
      "text": "no, none"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0031",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 227.87,
      "end_seconds": 232.48,
      "duration_seconds": 4.61,
      "text": "Do you react to to any medicines or foods? Any allergies?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0032",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 233.25,
      "end_seconds": 237.55,
      "duration_seconds": 4.3,
      "text": "Milk. I come out in... well, a rash."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0033",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 238.06,
      "end_seconds": 242.15,
      "duration_seconds": 4.09,
      "text": "Do you have any medical conditions I should know about?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0034",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 243.97,
      "end_seconds": 245.62,
      "duration_seconds": 1.65,
      "text": "no, no conditions"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0035",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 254.22,
      "end_seconds": 255.08,
      "duration_seconds": 0.86,
      "text": "any smoking?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0036",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 255.92,
      "end_seconds": 259.58,
      "duration_seconds": 3.66,
      "text": "No, I've never smoked in my life."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0037",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 261.65,
      "end_seconds": 263.01,
      "duration_seconds": 1.36,
      "text": "What about alcohol?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0038",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 267.98,
      "end_seconds": 272.44,
      "duration_seconds": 4.46,
      "text": "I'll have a glass of wine with dinner."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0039",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 273.73,
      "end_seconds": 276.61,
      "duration_seconds": 2.88,
      "text": "What do you do during the day?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0040",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 278.1,
      "end_seconds": 281.51,
      "duration_seconds": 3.41,
      "text": "I look after my grandchildren most days."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0041",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 282.41,
      "end_seconds": 284.49,
      "duration_seconds": 2.08,
      "text": "Is there someone at home?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0042",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 286.5,
      "end_seconds": 290.64,
      "duration_seconds": 4.14,
      "text": "My husband and I live above the shop."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0043",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 305.35,
      "end_seconds": 311.66,
      "duration_seconds": 6.31,
      "text": "okay, thinking it through, it points towards blood pressure above target on current treatment"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0044",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 314.27,
      "end_seconds": 315.82,
      "duration_seconds": 1.55,
      "text": "is this permanent?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0045",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 317.78,
      "end_seconds": 330.1,
      "duration_seconds": 12.32,
      "text": "It's reasonable to be concerned, but right now blood pressure above target on current treatment is my leading thought, not anything worse. We should do an ECG for hypertension."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0046",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 331.66,
      "end_seconds": 333.74,
      "duration_seconds": 2.08,
      "text": "Is that done today?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0047",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 337.56,
      "end_seconds": 344.67,
      "duration_seconds": 7.11,
      "text": "For this, amlodipine, 5 milligrams, once a day, long term. That That should help with blood pressure."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0048",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 345.27,
      "end_seconds": 348.1,
      "duration_seconds": 2.83,
      "text": "Should I take that with food?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0049",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 348.96,
      "end_seconds": 365.96,
      "duration_seconds": 17.0,
      "text": "Cut down on salty foods and keep a home blood pressure diary. Kidney function blood tests is something we might do if this doesn't improve in two weeks. I think we're done unless you have questions."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0050",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 367.63,
      "end_seconds": 371.39,
      "duration_seconds": 3.76,
      "text": "Okay, that makes sense. Thanks for explaining."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0051",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 372.77,
      "end_seconds": 373.99,
      "duration_seconds": 1.22,
      "text": "Take care now."
    }
  ]
}